<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fath Ali Khan Afshar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1763">1763</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fath Ali Khan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afshar-tribe">Afshar</a> was the khan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urmia">Urmia</a> and a leading contender for power in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> in 1747. He fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azad-khan-afghan">Azad Khan Afghan</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> Mohammad Hasan Khan and for a time controlled much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karim-khan-zand">Karim Khan Zand</a> besieged Urmia in 1762, took him prisoner and had him put to death.</p></div>
